-mi-ee","الحرم الجامعي"],["tuition fees","rusoom dirasiyya","roo-SOOM di-raa-SEE-ya","الرسوم الدراسية"],["semester","fasl dirasi","fasl di-RAA-see","الفصل الدراسي"],["course","maadda","MAAD-da","المادة"],["essay","maqaala","ma-GAA-la","المقالة"],["thesis","risaala","ri-SAA-la","الرسالة"],["diploma","diblom","dib-LOM","الدبلوم"],["seminar","nadwa","NAD-wa","الندوة"],["entrance exam","ikhtibaar qabool","ikh-ti-BAAR ga-BOOL","اختبار القبول"],["application","talab","TA-lab","الطلب"],["student card","bitaaqat taalib","bi-TAA-gat TAA-lib","بطاقة طالب"]]},{"id":"school-verbs","title":"School verbs","items":[["to study","adris","AD-ris","أدرس"],["to teach","adarris","a-DAR-ris","أدرّس"],["to ask","as'al","AS-al","أسأل"],["to answer","ajaawib","a-jaa-WIB","أجاوب"],["to repeat","u'eed","oo-EED","أعيد"],["to understand","afham","AF-ham","أفهم"],["to remember","atdhakkar","at-DHAK-kar","أتذكر"],["to forget","ansa","AN-sa","أنسى"],["to explain","ashrah","ASH-rah","أشرح"],["to practise","atdarrab","at-DAR-rab","أتدرب"],["to pass an exam","anjah fi l-ikhtibaar","AN-jah fil ikh-ti-BAAR","أنجح في الاختبار"],["to fail an exam","arsib fi l-ikhtibaar","AR-sib fil ikh-ti-BAAR","أرسب في الاختبار"],["to write down","aktib","AK-tib","أكتب"],["to listen","asma'","AS-ma","أسمع"],["to read aloud","aqra bi-sawt 'aali","AG-ra bi-SAWT AA-lee","أقرأ بصوت عالي"],["to think","afakkir","a-FAK-kir","أفكر"],["to count","a'idd","A-idd","أعد"],["to spell","atahajja","a-ta-HAJ-ja","أتهجى"],["to translate","atarjim","a-TAR-jim","أترجم"],["to graduate","atkharraj","at-KHAR-raj","أتخرج"]],"note":"Shown as \"I ...\" (the verb for \"I\")."}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Gulf Arabic has separate words for you (m) and you (f). There is no word for \"am / is / are\" in the present: just put the pronoun and the word together."],"rows":[["I","ana"],["you (m)","inta"],["you (f)","inti"],["he","huwa"],["she","hiya"],["we","ihna"],["you all","intu"],["they","hum"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ana taalib","","أنا طالب"],["you are tall (m)","inta tawiil","","إنت طويل"],["she is my sister","hiya ukhti","","هي أختي"],["we are friends","ihna asdigaa'","","احنا أصدقاء"],["they are teachers","hum mudarrisiin","","هم مدرسين"],["he is a teacher","huwa mudarris","HOO-wa mu-DAR-ris","هو مدرس"],["you (plural) are students","intu tullaab","IN-too tul-LAAB","انتو طلاب"],["I am happy","ana mabsoot","A-na mab-SOOT","أنا مبسوط"],["you are my friend (m)","inta sadeegi","IN-ta sa-DEE-gi","إنت صديقي"],["she is at school","hiya fi l-madrasa","HI-ya fil mad-RA-sa","هي في المدرسة"],["we are in Dubai","ihna fi dubai","ih-NA fee du-BAI","احنا في دبي"],["you are my sister (f)","inti ukhti","IN-ti UKH-ti","إنتي أختي"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Arabic has singular, dual (two) and plural. Many plurals are irregular, so learn them with the word. People often end in -iin, things in -aat."],"rows":[["two of something","add -ain (kitaab, kitaabain)"],["people (m)","add -iin (mudarris, mudarrisiin)"],["things (f)","add -aat (sayyaara, sayyaaraat)"]],"ex":[["book, books","kitaab, kutub","","كتاب، كتب"],["house, houses","bayt, buyoot","","بيت، بيوت"],["boy, boys","walad, awlaad","","ولد، أولاد"],["girl, girls","bint, banaat","","بنت، بنات"],["friend, friends","sadiig, asdigaa'","","صديق، أصدقاء"],["car, cars","sayyaara, sayyaaraat","","سيارة، سيارات"],["teachers (m)","mudarrisiin","","مدرسين"],["two books","kitaabain","","كتابين"],["room, rooms","ghurfa, ghuraf","GHUR-fa GHU-raf","غرفة، غرف"],["city, cities","madeena, mudun","ma-DEE-na MU-dun","مدينة، مدن"],["student, students","taalib, tullaab","TAA-lib tul-LAAB","طالب، طلاب"],["day, days","yoom, ayyaam","yoom ay-YAAM","يوم، أيام"],["street, streets","shaari', shawaari'","SHAA-ri sha-WAA-ri","شارع، شوارع"],["key, keys","miftaah, mafaateeh","mif-TAAH ma-faa-TEEH","مفتاح، مفاتيح"],["dog, dogs","kalb, kilaab","kalb ki-LAAB","كلب، كلاب"],["chair, chairs","kursi, karaasi","KUR-si ka-RAA-si","كرسي، كراسي"]]},{"id":"possessives-my-your","title":"Possessives: my, your...","text":["Add a short ending to the noun. The noun after it has no \"the\"."],"rows":[["my","-i (bayti = my house)"],["your (m)","-ak (baytak)"],["your (f)","-ich (baytich)"],["his","-ah (baytah)"],["her","-ha (baytha)"],["our","-na (baytna)"],["their","-hum (baythum)"]],"ex":[["my house","bayti","","بيتي"],["your name (m)","ismak","","اسمك"],["your car (f)","sayyaartich","","سيارتج"],["his father","abuuh","","أبوه"],["our school","madrastna","","مدرستنا"],["your book (m)","kitaabak","ki-TAA-bak","كتابك"],["her name","ismha","IS-ma","اسمها"],["their house","baythum","BAYT-hum","بيتهم"],["our teacher","mudarrisna","mu-DAR-ris-na","مدرسنا"],["my mother","ummi","UM-mi","أمي"],["your phone (m)","telefoonak","te-le-FOO-nak","تلفونك"],["his friend","sadeegah","sa-DEE-gah","صديقه"]]},{"id":"there-is-i-have","title":"There is, I have","text":["Use \"fii\" for there is, and \"'ind\" + ending for have. Say it with \"ma\" to make it negative."],"rows":[["there is","fii"],["there is not","ma fii"],["I have","'indi"],["you have (m)","'indak"],["you have (f)","'indich"],["he has","'indah"],["we have","'indna"]],"ex":[["there is a problem","fii mushkila","","في مشكلة"],["there is no water","ma fii maay","","ما في ماي"],["I have a car","'indi sayyaara","","عندي سيارة"],["I do not have time","ma 'indi wagt","","ما عندي وقت"],["she has two brothers","'indha akhwaan","","عندها أخوان"],["there is a lesson today","fii daris il-yoom","fee DA-ris il YOOM","في درس اليوم"],["there is no teacher","ma fii mudarris","ma fee mu-DAR-ris","ما في مدرس"],["I have a brother","'indi akh","IN-di akh","عندي أخ"],["she has a car","'indha sayyaara","IN-dha say-YAA-ra","عندها سيارة"],["do you have a pen? (m)","'indak galam","IN-dak GA-lam","عندك قلم؟"],["we have an exam","'indna ikhtibaar","IN-na ikh-ti-BAAR","عندنا اختبار"],["they have a big house","'indhum bayt kabiir","IN-hum bayt ka-BEER","عندهم بيت كبير"]]},{"id":"the-verb-present-tense","title":"The verb: present tense","text":["The beginning of the verb shows the person. Pattern with the verb \"to go\" (rooh):"],"rows":[["I go","arooh"],["you go (m)","tirooh"],["you go (f)","tirooh-iin"],["he goes","yirooh"],["she goes","tirooh"],["we go","nirooh"],["they go","yiroohoon"]],"ex":[["I go to school","arooh il-madrasa","","أروح المدرسة"],["he eats rice","yaakul rizz","","ياكل رز"],["we drink coffee","nishrab gahwa","","نشرب قهوة؟"],["she works in a bank","tishtaghil fi bank","","تشتغل في بنك"],["where do you go? (m)","wayn tirooh","","وين تروح؟"],["I drink water","ashrab maay","ASH-rab maay","أشرب ماي"],["he writes a letter","yaktib risaala","YAK-tib ri-SAA-la","يكتب رسالة"],["we study Arabic","nidris 'arabi","NID-ris AA-ra-bee","ندرس عربي"],["they play football","yil'abuun kurat il-qadam","yil-A-boon KOO-rat il GA-dam","يلعبون كرة القدم"],["she reads a book","tiqra kitaab","TIG-ra ki-TAAB","تقرأ كتاب"],["I know the answer","a'rif il-jawaab","AR-if il ja-WAAB","أعرف الجواب"],["you speak English (m)","tihki inglizi","TIH-ki in-GLEE-zee","تحكي إنجليزي"],["I live in Dubai","askun fi dubai","AS-kun fee du-BAI","أسكن في دبي"]]},{"id":"past-and-future","title":"Past and future","text":["Past: the verb ends with -t for \"I\". Future: put \"ba-\" or \"bi-\" before the present verb (Gulf), or use \"raH\"."],"rows":[["I went","ruht"],["I ate","akalt"],["I saw","shift"],["I will go","barooh"],["I will see","bashoof"]],"ex":[["I went yesterday","ruht imbaarih","","رحت إمبارح"],["I ate rice","akalt rizz","","أكلت رز"],["I saw him","shiftah","","شفته"],["I will go tomorrow","barooh bukra","","بروح بكرة"],["I will call you","batisil bik","","بتصل بك"],["I studied last night","darast il-baarha bi-l-layl","da-RAST il BAA-ri-ha bil LAYL","درست البارحة بالليل"],["she wrote the lesson","katabat id-dars","KA-ta-bat id DARS","كتبت الدرس"],["we travelled to Oman","safarna 'umaan","sa-FAR-na u-MAAN","سافرنا عمان"],["they came yesterday","jaw imbaarih","JAW im-BAA-rih","جاو إمبارح"],["I will study tomorrow","badris bukra","bad-RIS BOOK-ra","بدرس بكرة"],["he will come later","bijii ba'dayn","bi-JEE ba-DAYN","بيجي بعدين"],["we will eat at eight","binaakul as-saa'a thamaanya","bi-NAA-kul as SAA-a tha-MAA-nya","بناكل الساعة ثمانية"]]},{"id":"please-can-want","title":"Please, can, want","text":["Useful starters: abgha (I want), agdar (I can), laazim (I must)."],"rows":[["I want","abgha"],["I can","agdar"],["I must","laazim"],["do you want...?","tabgha"]],"ex":[["I want water","abgha maay","","أبغي ماي"],["can I sit?","agdar ag'ud","","أقدر أقعد؟"],["I must go","laazim arooh","","لازم أروح"],["do you want tea?","tabgha chaay","","تبغي شاي؟"],["I cannot","ma agdar","","ما أقدر"],["I want a coffee","abgha gahwa","AB-gha GAH-wa","أبغي قهوة"],["I can speak Arabic","agdar ahki 'arabi","AG-dar AH-ki AA-ra-bee","أقدر أحكي عربي"],["you must study (m)","laazim tidris","LAA-zim TID-ris","لازم تدرس"],["do you want to come? (m)","tabgha tijii?","TAB-gha ti-JEE","تبغي تجي؟"],["she wants to go","tabgha tirooh","TAB-gha ti-ROOH","تبغى تروح"],["we cannot wait","ma nagdar nintathir","ma NAG-dar nin-TA-thir","ما نقدر ننتظر"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Word order is flexible. There is no \"is / am / are\": say the two words together. The adjective comes after the noun and agrees with it."],"rows":[["noun + adjective","bayt kabiir (a big house)"],["pronoun + noun","ana taalib (I student = I am a student)"],["verb first is also fine","aakul rizz (I eat rice)"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ana taalib","","أنا طالب"],["the house is big","il-bayt kabiir","","البيت كبير"],["she is a teacher","hiya mudarrisa","","هي مدرسة"],["I eat rice","aakul rizz","","آكل رز"],["this is my car","hadhi sayyaarti","","هذي سيارتي"],["the teacher is here","il-mudarris hina","il mu-DAR-ris HI-na","المدرس هنا"],["the car is new","is-sayyaara jadeeda","is say-YAA-ra ja-DEE-da","السيارة جديدة"],["I drink tea every day","ashrab chaay kull yoom","ASH-rab CHAAY kull yoom","أشرب شاي كل يوم"],["Dubai is a big city","dubai madeena kabeera","du-BAI ma-DEE-na ka-BEE-ra","دبي مدينة كبيرة"],["the weather is hot","il-jaw haar","il JAW haar","الجو حار"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Use \"ma\" before a verb. Use \"mu\" before an adjective or noun.","Use \"ma\" before a verb. Use \"mu\" before an adjective or noun. Always show the positive too."],"rows":[["not (verb)","ma + verb"],["not (adjective)","mu + word"]],"ex":[["I want","abgha","AB-gha","أبغي"],["I do not want","ma abgha","ma AB-gha","ما أبغي"],["I speak English","ahki inglizi","AH-ki in-GLEE-zee","أحكي إنجليزي"],["I do not speak English","ma ahki inglizi","ma AH-ki in-GLEE-zee","ما أحكي إنجليزي"],["I like it","yi'jibni","yi-JIB-ni","يعجبني"],["I do not like it","ma yi'jibni","ma yi-JIB-ni","ما يعجبني"],["she is here","hiya hina","HI-ya HI-na","هي هنا"],["she is not here","hiya mu hina","HI-ya moo HI-na","هي مو هنا"],["I have a car","'indi sayyaara","IN-di say-YAA-ra","عندي سيارة"],["I do not have a car","ma 'indi sayyaara","ma IN-di say-YAA-ra","ما عندي سيارة"],["I understand","afham","AF-ham","أفهم"],["I do not understand","ma afham","ma AF-ham","ما أفهم"],["we are tired","ihna ta'baanin","ih-NA ta-BAA-neen","احنا تعبانين"],["we are not tired","ihna mu ta'baanin","ih-NA moo ta-BAA-neen","احنا مو تعبانين"],["he works on Sundays","yishtaghil yoom al-ahad","yish-TA-ghil yoom al A-had","يشتغل يوم الأحد"],["he does not work on Sundays","ma yishtaghil yoom al-ahad","ma yish-TA-ghil yoom al A-had","ما يشتغل يوم الأحد"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: say a normal sentence with a rising voice. You can also start with \"hal\" (more formal)."],"rows":[["statement","inta taalib"],["question","inta taalib?"],["more formal","hal inta taalib?"]],"ex":[["are you a student? (m)","inta taalib","","إنت طالب"],["do you speak English?","tihki inglizi","","تحكي إنجليزي؟"],["do you have time? (m)","'indak wagt","","عندك وقت؟"],["is it far?","ba'iid","","بعيد"],["do you want tea? (m)","tabgha chaay","","تبغي شاي؟"],["is she a teacher?","hiya mudarrisa","HI-ya mu-DAR-ri-sa","هي مدرسة؟"],["are you tired? (m)","inta ta'baan","IN-ta ta-BAAN","إنت تعبان؟"],["is the restaurant open?","il-mat'am maftooh","il MAT-am maf-TOOH","المطعم مفتوح؟"],["do you speak Arabic? (m)","tihki 'arabi","TIH-ki AA-ra-bee","تحكي عربي؟"],["are you from the Emirates? (m)","inta min il-imaaraat","IN-ta min il i-maa-RAAT","إنت من الإمارات؟"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","shu"],["where","wayn"],["when","mita"],["why","layish"],["how","shlon"],["who","min"],["how much","kam / bikam"]],"ex":[["what is this?","shu hadha","","شو هذا؟"],["where is the hotel?","wayn il-funduq","","وين الفندق؟"],["when does it open?","mita yiftah","","متى يفتح؟"],["why are you late?","layish mit'akhkhir","","ليش متأخر؟"],["how are you? (m)","shlonak","","شلونك؟"],["who is he?","min huwa","min HOO-wa","من هو؟"],["what is your name? (m)","shu ismak","shoo IS-mak","شو اسمك؟"],["where do you live? (m)","wayn taskun","wayn TAS-kun","وين تسكن؟"],["how much is this?","bikam hadha","bi-KAM HA-dha","بكم هذا؟"],["why are you angry? (m)","layish zi'laan","LAY-ish zi-LAAN","ليش زعلان؟"],["when is the exam?","mita il-ikhtibaar","MI-ta il ikh-ti-BAAR","متى الاختبار؟"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Show respect with titles and polite forms. Friends use short, warm words. Always use the right gender."],"rows":[["casual hello","hala"],["formal hello","as-salaamu 'alaykum"],["casual \"you\"","inta / inti"],["very formal \"you\"","hadritak"],["casual \"please\"","min fadlak"],["polite \"please, go ahead\"","tafaddal"]],"ex":[["hello (casual)","hala","","هلا"],["peace be upon you (formal)","as-salaamu 'alaykum","","السلام عليكم"],["how are you? (polite)","kayf haalak","","كيف حالك؟"],["please, come in","tafaddal","","تفضل"],["thank you very much","shukran jaziilan","","شكراً جزيلاً"],["good morning","sabaah il-khayr","sa-BAAH il KHAYR","صباح الخير"],["good morning (reply)","sabaah in-noor","sa-BAAH in NOOR","صباح النور"],["how are you? (informal)","shlonak","SHLO-nak","شلونك؟"],["welcome","ahlan wa sahlan","AH-lan wa SAH-lan","أهلاً وسهلاً"],["thank you, sir","shukran ya ustaadh","SHOOK-ran ya oos-TAADH","شكراً يا أستاذ"],["excuse me, sir","'an idhnak ya ustaadh","an IDH-nak ya oos-TAADH","عن إذنك يا أستاذ"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["To give an order use the \"you\" form of the verb without the pronoun. Make it negative with \"la\". Add -u for a group."],"rows":[["come! (m)","ta'aal","ta-AAL","تعال"],["come! (f)","ta'aali","ta-AA-li","تعالي"],["do not come!","la tijii","la ti-JEE","لا تجي"]],"ex":[["come here","ta'aal hina","ta-AAL HI-na","تعال هنا"],["do not come here","la tijii hina","la ti-JEE HI-na","لا تجي هنا"],["sit down","ij-lis","IJ-lis","اجلس"],["do not sit down","la tijlis","la TIJ-lis","لا تجلس"],["be quiet","uskut","US-kut","اسكت"],["do not be late","la titakhkhar","la ti-TAKH-khar","لا تتأخر"],["open the door","iftah il-baab","IF-tah il BAAB","افتح الباب"],["close the window","sakkir ish-shubbaak","SAK-kir ish shub-BAAK","سكّر الشباك"],["listen to me","isma' minni","IS-ma MIN-ni","اسمع مني"],["do not worry","la tiqlag","la TIG-lag","لا تقلق"],["speak slowly","ihki bi-shwaysh","IH-ki bish-WAYSH","احكي بشويش"],["wait a moment","istanna shwayya","is-TAN-na SHWAY-ya","استنى شوية"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["agdar = I can, laazim = must, abgha = I want. All are followed by the verb for \"I\" (or \"you\", \"he\") without \"to\". \"ma\" makes them negative; \"mamnoo'\" = forbidden."],"rows":[["I can","agdar","AG-dar","أقدر"],["I must","laazim","LAA-zim","لازم"],["I want","abgha","AB-gha","أبغي"]],"ex":[["I can swim","agdar asbah","AG-dar AS-bah","أقدر أسبح"],["I cannot swim","ma agdar asbah","ma AG-dar AS-bah","ما أقدر أسبح"],["can you help me?","tagdar tsaa'idni","TAG-dar tsaa-ID-ni","تقدر تساعدني؟"],["we must go","laazim nirooh","LAA-zim ni-ROOH","لازم نروح"],["we must not go","mamnoo' nirooh","mam-NOO ni-ROOH","ممنوع نروح"],["I want to eat","abgha aakul","AB-gha AA-kul","أبغي آكل"],["I do not want to eat","ma abgha aakul","ma AB-gha AA-kul","ما أبغي آكل"],["you can come","tagdar tijii","TAG-dar ti-JEE","تقدر تجي"],["you cannot come","ma tagdar tijii","ma TAG-dar ti-JEE","ما تقدر تجي"],["she wants to study","tabgha tidris","TAB-gha TID-ris","تبغى تدرس"],["I must work today","laazim ashtaghil il-yoom","LAA-zim ash-TA-ghil il YOOM","لازم أشتغل اليوم"],["you must not run","mamnoo' tijri","mam-NOO TIJ-ri","ممنوع تجري"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["fi = in / at; 'ala = on; taht = under; jamb = next to; gareeb min = near. In Arabic the noun after these words usually has \"il-\" (the)."],"rows":[["in / at","fi","fee","في"],["on","'ala","ala","على"],["under","taht","taht","تحت"],["next to","jamb","jamb","جنب"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","il-kitaab 'ala it-taawla","il ki-TAAB ala it TAAW-la","الكتاب على الطاولة"],["the cat is under the table","il-bisse taht it-taawla","il BIS-se taht it TAAW-la","البسة تحت الطاولة"],["I am at school","ana fi l-madrasa","A-na fil mad-RA-sa","أنا في المدرسة"],["I am at home","ana fi l-bayt","A-na fil BAYT","أنا في البيت"],["the shop is next to the bank","id-dukkaan jamb il-bank","id dook-KAAN jamb il BANK","الدكان جنب البنك"],["the park is near the station","il-hadeeqa gareeba min il-mahatta","il ha-DEE-ga ga-REE-ba min il ma-HAT-ta","الحديقة قريبة من المحطة"],["we meet in the morning","nitlaaga is-subuh","nit-LAA-ga is SOO-boh","نتلاقى الصبح"],["the lesson is at nine","id-dars as-saa'a tis'a","id DARS as SAA-a TIS-a","الدرس الساعة تسعة"],["the key is in the bag","il-miftaah fi sh-shanta","il mif-TAAH fish SHAN-ta","المفتاح في الشنطة"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add a- to the front of the adjective for \"more\" (akbar = bigger / the biggest). Use \"min\" for \"than\": akbar min."],"rows":[["bigger than","akbar min","AK-bar min","أكبر من"],["better","ahsan","AH-san","أحسن"],["the biggest","al-akbar","al AK-bar","الأكبر"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","kabiir, akbar, al-akbar","ka-BEER AK-bar al AK-bar","كبير، أكبر، الأكبر"],["small, smaller, the smallest","sagheer, asghar, al-asghar","sa-GHEER AS-ghar al AS-ghar","صغير، أصغر، الأصغر"],["this is better than that","hadha ahsan min dhaak","HA-dha AH-san min DHAAK","هذا أحسن من ذاك"],["this is worse than that","hadha awda' min dhaak","HA-dha AW-da min DHAAK","هذا أسوأ من ذاك"],["she is taller than me","hiya atwal minni","HI-ya AT-wal MIN-ni","هي أطول مني"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","tashkand akbar min samarqand","tash-KAND AK-bar min sa-mar-KAND","طشقند أكبر من سمرقند"],["it is the cheapest","hadha arkhas shay","HA-dha AR-khas shay","هذا أرخص شي"],["the same as","zayy","zayy","زي"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","huwa mudarris","HOO-wa mu-DAR-ris","هو مدرس"],["you (plural) are students","intu tullaab","IN-too tul-LAAB","انتو طلاب"],["I am happy","ana mabsoot","A-na mab-SOOT","أنا مبسوط"],["she is at school","hiya fi l-madrasa","HI-ya fil mad-RA-sa","هي في المدرسة"],["you are my friend","inta sadeegi","IN-ta sa-DEE-gi","إنت صديقي"],["it is cold","il-jaw baarid","il JAW BAA-rid","الجو بارد"],["I study English","adris inglizi","AD-ris in-GLEE-zee","أدرس إنجليزي"],["he teaches maths","yadarris riyaadiyyaat","ya-DAR-ris ree-yaa-DEE-yaat","يدرس رياضيات"],["they work every day","yishtaghluun kull yoom","yish-TAGH-loon kull yoom","يشتغلون كل يوم"],["is this your book?","hadha kitaabak","HA-dha ki-TAA-bak","هذا كتابك؟"],["are they here?","hum hina","hum HI-na","هم هنا؟"],["do you like tea?","tihibb chaay","ti-HIBB CHAAY","تحب شاي؟"],["what time is it?","kam is-saa'a","kam is SAA-a","كم الساعة؟"],["whose book is this?","hadha kitaab min","HA-dha ki-TAAB min","هذا كتاب من؟"],["how old are you?","kam 'umrak","kam UM-rak","كم عمرك؟"],["how do you say it?","shlon tigool","shlon ti-GOOL","شلون تقول؟"],["your book (formal)","kitaabkum","ki-TAAB-kum","كتابكم"],["their house","baythum","BAYT-hum","بيتهم"],["my phone","telefooni","te-le-FOO-ni","تلفوني"],["excuse me, sir","'an idhnak ya ustaadh","an IDH-nak ya oos-TAADH","عن إذنك يا أستاذ"],["please sit down (formal)","tafaddal ij-lis","ta-FAD-dal IJ-lis","تفضل اجلس"],["come here (informal)","ta'aal hina","ta-AAL HI-na","تعال هنا"],["yesterday I was tired","imbaarih kunt ta'baan","im-BAA-rih kunt ta-BAAN","إمبارح كنت تعبان"],["I will study tomorrow","badris bukra","bad-RIS BOOK-ra","بدرس بكرة"],["we went to the park","ruhna il-hadeeqa","ROOH-na il ha-DEE-ga","رحنا الحديقة"]]}],"name":"Khaleeji Arabic","id":"khl","flag":"ae","script":"Arabic","note":""}